GAL16V8
6502 Vect

V1   V2   S0   S1   S2   NC   NC   NC   NC   GND
VPB  NC   NC   NC   VIRQ A4   A3   A2   A1   VCC

A1.T = VIRQ*S0 + /VIRQ*V1
A1.E = VPB
A2.T = VIRQ*S1 + /VIRQ*V2
A2.E = VPB
A3.T = VIRQ*S2 + /VIRQ
A3.E = VPB
A4.T = /VIRQ
A4.E = VPB 

DESCRIPTION

This is the vector address selection logic. On the main board, the 6502's
A4..1 address lines are connected to tristate buffers whose outputs are 
connected to A4..1 of the memory units. These buffers are in the high 
impedance state whenever VPB is low. This is designed to allow a separate
module to provide vectored interrupt support.

The V1 and V2 inputs to this logic are the 6502's A1 and A2 address lines.
The S2..0 inputs represent the decoded address output of the priority decoder, 
which specifies requested IRQ vector.

THe A4..1 outputs of this logic have tristate outputs that are controlled
by VPB. The outputs are driven only when VPB is low. The logic is designed
to output the appropriate vector address based on the state of V1 and V12.
Bits A15..5 as well as A0 of the vector address are all provided by the 6502.
 Bits A4..1 are provided by this logic based on V1 and V2 as follows.

 V2 V1 S2 S1 S0  Vector  Description
  0  1  X  X  X  FFFA	 Non-maskable interrupt (NMI)
  1  0  X  X  X	 FFFC	 System reset (RESET)
  1  1  0  0  0  FFE0    Interrupt request 0 (IRQ0)	
  1  1  0  0  1  FFE2    Interrupt request 1 (IRQ1)	
  1  1  0  1  0  FFE4    Interrupt request 2 (IRQ2)	
  1  1  0  1  1  FFE6    Interrupt request 3 (IRQ3)	
  1  1  1  0  0  FFE8    Interrupt request 4 (IRQ4)	
  1  1  1  0  1  FFEA    Interrupt request 5 (IRQ5)	
  1  1  1  0  1  FFEC    Interrupt request 6 (IRQ6)	
  1  1  1  1  1  FFEE    Interrupt request 7 (IRQ7)	
